                <pb facs="0046" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v15/pg14"/>

                <head>3. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On July 22, the NSC Planning Board completed
                        NSC 5909, “U.S. Policy Toward South Asia,” a
                    draft statement of policy on the subject which, if adopted by the NSC, was intended to supersede NSC 5701. The paper was transmitted to the NSC that same day, under cover of a memorandum by
                        James Lay; it was scheduled for
                    consideration by the Council at its meeting of August 6. (Department of State,
                        S/S–NSC
                    Files: Lot 63 D 351, NSC 5909)</p>
                <pb facs="0047" n="15" xml:id="pg15"/>
                <p>NSC 5909 was discussed by the NSC at meetings on August 6 and August 18; see <ref
                        target="#d4"><hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi></ref> and <ref target="#d5"
                        >Document 5</ref>. An amended version of the paper was approved by the
                    President and circulated as NSC 5909/1 on August
                    21. NSC 5909/1 is printed as <ref target="#d6"
                        >Document 6</ref>.</p>
            </div>
